  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 16,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.689,
            0.048,
            0.86,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fractions in Disguise"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.848,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Kishanlal (retailer) buys sweaters from a wholesaler at a price of ₹300 per sweater. The marked price he quotes his customers is ₹480. After bargaining, he sells this sweater at ₹430. Notice that the selling price is greater than the cost price, resulting in a profit of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "430-\\bar{x}300=\\bar{x}130"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . If the selling price is less than the cost price, it will result in a loss."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.192,
            0.847,
            0.23
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Example 4: Find out the percentage profit Kishanlal made on this sweater. 0 300 430"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.235,
            0.525,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We shall consider the cost price to be 100% to find out the percentage profit made with reference to the cost price. The following rough diagram describes this situation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.332,
            0.411,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The profit amount is ₹130."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.219,
            0.85,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 5,
              "bbox": [
                0.535,
                0.219,
                0.85,
                0.341
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_5.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.358,
            0.562,
            0.384
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The percentage profit is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{130}{300} \\times 100 = 43.3\\%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.392,
            0.802,
            0.416
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Find the profit percentage of the wholesaler and the manufacturer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.429,
            0.847,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Shambhavi owns a stationery shop. She procures 200 page notebooks at ₹36 per book. She sells them with a profit margin of 20%. Find the selling price."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.501,
            0.846,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ She sells crayon boxes at ₹50 per box with a profit margin of 25%. How much did Shambhavi buy them from the wholesaler?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.557,
            0.847,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 5:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The rice stock in Raghu’s provision store is getting old. He had purchased the rice at ₹35 per kg. To clear his stock, he sells 10 kg rice"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.595,
            0.524,
            0.615
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "for ₹300. Find out the percentage loss."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.617,
            0.556,
            0.674
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The amount Raghu had paid towards buying the 10 kg rice is ₹350. He sold it for ₹300."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.68,
            0.434,
            0.699
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The loss is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "350 - 300 = 50"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.6,
            0.865,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.57,
                0.6,
                0.865,
                0.712
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_16_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.701,
            0.554,
            0.727
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The percentage loss is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{50}{350} \\times 100 = 14.28\\%."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.735,
            0.845,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Could we have just calculated the loss percentage per kg instead? Would it be the same?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.789,
            0.847,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 6:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Shyamala had procured decorative vases at ₹2650 per piece. One of the pieces was slightly damaged. She decides to sell it at a loss of 18%. How much will she get by selling this piece?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.854,
            0.845,
            0.893
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Try making an estimate. Draw a rough diagram depicting the given situation."
